+// level then puts a corner a rounding error outside, and clipHalfPlane emits an intersection at an arbitrary place
+// along each edge that lies on the plane. Each becomes a contact at the corners' depth, so the face's contacts go from
+// 4 to 6 or 8 and back from step to step, and with them the force the face carries. This is clipHalfPlane with a vertex
